Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:14:19 +0200
Subject: nv30: no A16 (X16) textures on the PS3

mpv --vo=gpu (0.41, --hwdec=no) on a 360p H.264 clip wedged the RSX at its first frame on
2026-10-28: graph exception 0x105, which no reset short of a console reboot recovers. mpv's
renderer on GL 2.1 runs in "dumb mode": one draw samples the three planes (L8, linear,
640x360 and 320x180) and a 64x64 dither texture, GL_LUMINANCE16, which nv30 stores as L16_UNORM
in NV40's A16 format (format 0x14, libgcm's X16), swizzled, sampled NEAREST with GL_REPEAT at
coordinates from gl_FragCoord. Run on the PC (mpv's renderer through libmpv on this Mesa under
qemu, the nouveau drm-shim answering like ps3rsx), its submit lines up word for word with the
PFIFO cache the PS3 dumped: the dither upload (SIFM 64x64, pitch 128), the state, the
texture units, the draw of 6 vertices, the timer query and the fence, and the exception came
after PGRAPH had taken the fence's release, so from the draw. Nothing had sampled the A16
format on the RSX before (gl-texfmt covers L8, A8, I8, 4444, 1555 and L8A8; the state tracker
picks L16, A16 or I16 only for the sized 16-bit internal formats, which games hardly use, and
R16 needs ARB_texture_rg, absent), and the rest of the draw is what games and glamor send.

On the PS3 is_format_supported now refuses sampler views of the formats that map to A16 (L16,
A16, I16, R16, unorm and snorm); the state tracker then takes L8, A8 or I8 (GL_LUMINANCE16:
L16, RGBA16, then L8). mpv's dither goes from 16 to 8 bits of resolution, which its output to
an 8-bit display hardly shows. ps3rsx's validator refuses the format now (texfmt_ok()).

Checked on the PC with the shim: mpv's first frame samples the dither texture as L8 (format
0x81), and ps3rsx's validator passes the submit (its host test, fixtures/mpv-vo-gpu-0x105.h).

Found by: docs/dumps/exception-0x105-mpv-vo-gpu.txt (video baseline for the browser)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c
@@ -330,6 +330,15 @@ nv30_screen_is_format_supported(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
        util_format_get_blocksize(format) == 2)
       return false;
 
+   /* PS3: the RSX raised graph exception 0x105, which wedges it until the console reboots, at
+    * the first draw that sampled the A16 format (libgcm's X16: L16, A16, I16 and R16), mpv's
+    * dither texture (GL_LUMINANCE16); nothing had sampled the format on the RSX before, and
+    * ps3rsx refuses it. Without it the state tracker takes the 8-bit format of the kind (L8
+    * for GL_LUMINANCE16). */
+   if (nv30_screen(pscreen)->base.is_ps3 && (bindings & PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW) &&
+       nv30_texfmt(pscreen, format)->nv40 == NV40_3D_TEX_FORMAT_FORMAT_A16)
+      return false;
+
    /* NV30_VTX_SNORM8: fetched as unsigned bytes, normalized by the vertex program */
    if ((bindings & PIPE_BIND_VERTEX_BUFFER) && nv30_screen(pscreen)->vtx_snorm8 &&
        nv30_snorm8_components(format)) {
